,8}]デカン-4-オン\n  * (1S,2S,3S,6R,8R,9S,10R)-2-benzoyl-1,3,8,10-tetrahydroxy-9-(4-methoxy-2-oxo-2H-pyran-6-yl)-5-oxatricyclo[4.3.1.0^{3,8}]decan-4-one\n\nその他の名称 (5件)：\n\n  * エンテロシン\n  * Enterocin\n  * (3R,8R)-7α-Benzoyl-4,4a,5,6,7,7a-hexahydro-4aα,6α,7aα,8-tetrahydroxy-5β-(4-methoxy-2-oxo-2H-pyran-6-yl)-3β,6-methanocyclopenta[c]pyran-1(3H)-one\n  * ブルガマイシン\n  * Vulgamycin\n\nCAS登録番号： 59678-46-5\n用途語 (1件)：\n\n抗細菌作用\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBiomimetic Approach\nToward Enterocin and Deoxyenterocin (https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.joc.8b02273)\nciteturn44search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Enterocin (vulgamycin) is a structurally remarkable natural product with significant antibiotic activity.\nPublisher: American Chemical Society\n\nReceived: September 02, 2018\n\nPublished Online: January 18, 2019\n\nPublished in Issue: February 01, 2019\n\n\nCopyright © 2018 American Chemical Society\n\nJournal of Organic Chemistry (2019) 84 (3): 1162–1175.\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1021/acs.joc.8b02273\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nEnterocin (vulgamycin) is a structurally remarkable natural product with significant antibiotic activity. The synthesis of a linear polyketide resembling a biosynthetic precursor was achieved using an unusual acyloin reaction. A diazo group was introduced as a protecting group for an enolizable ketone. We were unable to bring about the envisioned biomimetic aldol addition cascade and gained insights into the feasibility of this process by DFT calculations. As an alternative approach to enterocin, we developed a Cu-catalyzed intramolecular cyclopropanation followed by a MgI_{2}-induced fragmentation to install the 2-oxabicyclo[3.3.1]­nonane core of the natural product.\n\n## Visual Abstract\n\nImage: Graphic. Refer to the image caption for details.\n\nSubjects Lipids, Peptides and proteins, Aldehydes, Solvents, Mixtures\n\n## Supporting Information\n\nThe Supporting Information is available free of charge on the ACS Publications website at DOI: 10.1021/acs.joc.8b02273.\n\n  * X-ray data for compound 23 (CIF)\n\n  * Screening tables, ^{1}H and ^{13}C spectra for all new compounds, crystallographic data, procedures for the computational part, and geometries of the optimized structures (PDF)\n\n\nsifile1- cif file\n\nsifile2- pdf file\n\nYou do not currently have access to this content.\n\n### ACS Login\n\n\n## Article Metrics\n\nTotal Views 3,708\n\n1,651 Pageviews\n\n2,057 PDF Downloads\n\nSince 6/1/2026--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-Pyrone Polyketides from Streptomyces ambofaciens BI0048, an Endophytic Actinobacterial Strain Isolated from the Red Alga Laurencia glandulifera (https://www.mdpi.com/1660-3397/15/12/389/pdf?version=1513220856)\nciteturn44search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.9 years ago;   - **7:** Enterocin (vulgamycin); complex polycyclic structure with a phenyl substituent, multiple hydroxyl groups, and a methoxy-substituted α-pyrone ring.\n  - **3:** α-Pyrone-containing compound with a hydroxyl group and a branched alkyl side chain; the side-chain terminal carbon is labeled 11.\n  - **4:** α-Pyrone-containing compound with a hydroxyl group and a branched alkyl side chain; the side-chain terminal carbon is labeled 10.\n\n- **Bottom row, left to right:**\n  - **5:** Wailupemycin D; structure containing a hydroxyl-substituted fused aromatic ring, a phenyl substituent, and a hydroxyl- and carbonyl-substituted α-pyrone ring.\n  - **6:** Wailupemycin E; structure containing a hydroxyl-substituted fused aromatic ring, an additional phenyl substituent, and a hydroxyl- and carbonyl-substituted α-pyrone ring.\n  - **7:** Enterocin (vulgamycin); complex polycyclic structure with a phenyl substituent, multiple hydroxyl groups, and a methoxy-substituted α-pyrone ring. The figure labels this structure **7 R = OH**.\n  - **8:** 5-Deoxy-enterocin; the corresponding structure is la